  "sender": "STAFF_DEVELOPER",
  "directiveId": "DIR-059",
  "summary": "DIR-059 COMPLETE (S1-S5), zero backend/schema change. PROVEN DEFECTS FIXED: (1) platform.js:956 getUserJobApplications was literally 'return getTrackedJobs(userId)' so /dashboard/applied-jobs rendered KANBAN rows instead of the applications table - it now reads GET /api/jobs-data/applications/list; (2) the applications table has NO jobTitle/company/location/salary and getApplications() does a bare SELECT with no join, so AppliedJobs.jsx:55-63 read undefined fields and every row rendered blank - rows are now normalised AND enriched via getJobById(job_id) with appliedDate from created_at; (3) the table defaults status to PENDING (uppercase) while the UI counted === 'pending' (lowercase) so the tile could never match - an APPLICATION_STATUS_MAP now canonicalises the stored vocabulary and the tile counts the canonical 'applied' (Under Review); (4) withdrawal and Kanban promotion did not exist - withdrawal is now confirm-gated through the shared Cuba dialog (useConfirmDialog -> EnterpriseConfirmModal, no native window.confirm) calling DELETE /api/jobs-data/applications/:id with optimistic removal and rollback, and Track in Kanban uses createTrackedJob with the canonical applied status and is idempotent. BACKEND: no new route was needed - jobsData.js already exposes the owner-scoped list (:277), delete (:319, 404/403) and tracker routes. GATES: new suite 7/7; job regression 33/33; product matrix 756 pass/0 fail; eslint 0 errors; build exit 0 in 2.41s. HONEST LIMITS: enrichment is one getJobById per row (a joined backend projection would be cheaper); the Kanban already-tracked set is session-scoped because tracker ids differ from application ids. Doc: .bridge/evidence/dir059-implementation-evidence.md."
}